  "summary": "Restricts wallet periodic rebroadcast and mempool resubmission on startup or import to transactions originating from the wallet. Unconfirmed transactions that do not spend any wallet inputs (i.e. incoming payments) are skipped.",
  "problem": "Nodes leak network identity simply by passively running a wallet: if an attacker sends a low-fee transaction to a target address, the recipient node will rebroadcast it after a timeout or retain it across restarts, allowing observers to associate the node's IP address with the wallet.",
  "evidence": [
   "Fixes issue #3828 ('Clients leak IPs if they are recipients of a transaction'), open since 2014.",
   "PR description notes: 'rebroadcast of transactions paying the wallet (but not spending any wallet inputs) is a privacy leak, since anyone can generate these, choose a low fee, and observe who rebroadcasts them.'"
