  "card": "Restricts wallet rebroadcasting and startup mempool resubmission exclusively to transactions originating from the wallet (`IsFromMe`). Currently, running a wallet passively rebroadcasts unconfirmed incoming transactions, enabling an attacker to identify a node's IP address by sending low-fee transactions to an address and watching for rebroadcasts or probing mempool retention across restarts. This resolves long-standing issue #3828, with the tradeoff that recipients must manually resubmit stuck incoming payments if the sender does not rebroadcast.",
